## Why This Is Asked
This question probes multi-tenant CNF provenance at scale, including per-tenant keys, drift detection, rollback, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped key management
- Per-tenant SBOMs and provenance enforcement
- ImagePolicyWebhook + OPA constraints
- Drift detection and tenant-aware rollback
- Observability: metrics, traces, audit logs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify image provenance per tenant
async function verifyProvenance(imageRef, tenant) {
  const sigOk = await cosign.verify(imageRef, { key: `kms://${tenant}-key` });
  const sbom = await fetchSBOM(imageRef);
  if (sbom.tenant !== tenant) throw new Error('Tenant SBOM mismatch');
  return sigOk;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate tenant keys without downtime?
- How would you test drift detection across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable, isolated QoS for multi-tenant CNFs with real-time config updates.

## Key Concepts
- Hierarchical token bucket, per-tenant and per-path
- Dynamic priority scheduling and cross-tenant isolation
- Fast policy propagation and SLA metrics
- Kubernetes manifests and minimal tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token bucket checker
class TB {
  constructor(cap, ref) { this.cap = cap; this.refill = ref; }
  consume(n=1){ if(this.cap>=n){ this.cap-=n; return true;} return false; }
  refillAt(now){ this.cap = Math.min(this.max, this.cap + (now-this.last)*this.fillRate); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test SLA adherence under bursty traffic?
- How would you roll out policy changes safely across clusters?

